      "content": "i get what you mean about the electronics, but maybe it's not about the plants themselves having wires in them. what if they are just using the specific density and surface area of the leaves to focus or reflect sound toward hidden mics? if you look at the way the leaves are angled in that circle, it almost looks like a parabolic setup. could that kind of biological geometry actually help with sound collection if there was some tech tucked into the soil or the pots?",
